WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.354
A Transferable Variant Signal That Grocery
Retrieval Cannot Reach.

00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:08.275
In automated checkout, a camera sees a shopper
lift a product.

00:00:08.275 --> 00:00:09.849
What goes in the cart?

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:14.901
Multimodal product retrieval matches the
photograph to a written catalog entry.

00:00:15.361 --> 00:00:19.585
The frozen model encodes each photo and each
description as a vector.

00:00:19.795 --> 00:00:24.809
For this Campbell’s Creamy Tomato soup, cosine
similarity ranks Chicken Noodle first.

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:28.156
Did the image features lose the flavor?

00:00:28.156 --> 00:00:31.455
A linear probe reads variants from those same

00:00:31.455 --> 00:00:35.167
features with 97.1 percent balanced accuracy on
seen brands.

00:00:35.627 --> 00:00:40.619
To test what carries over, average the photo
vectors for each variant of a training brand.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:42.125
Subtract that brand’s center.

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:46.013
Each arrow now shows how a variant differs from
its own brand.

00:00:46.473 --> 00:00:49.140
Stack these differences across training brands.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:54.473
A singular value decomposition finds the
directions along which variants differ most.

00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:56.210
We keep 64 directions.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.118
They span the variant subspace.

00:00:58.578 --> 00:00:59.867
Freeze those axes.

00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:05.021
Project a new brand’s images and descriptions
onto them, normalize, and compare.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:09.423
For these ten Sumatra photos, the mean points
closest to Sumatra.

00:01:09.423 --> 00:01:12.090
Shuffle the training labels within each brand,

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.615
and Pike Place wins.

00:01:14.075 --> 00:01:17.701
Over ten splits, the learned subspace beats
shuffled

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:21.328
labels by 13.6 percentage points across the
catalog.

00:01:21.538 --> 00:01:24.802
Within a brand, the gain falls to 3.9 points.

00:01:24.802 --> 00:01:27.703
Much of what transfers helps tell brands apart.

00:01:27.703 --> 00:01:29.879
The full embedding still retrieves best.
